    "notes": "Battery adapter lead: the Tamiya mate (C04) on the pack top to a JST VHR-2N housing (C05) on J1. POLARITY, in plain words: on the board J1 pin 1 is GND and pin 2 is BAT+ (ruling PB20; silk \"-\" at pin 1, \"+\" at pin 2), so the black battery-minus wire goes in housing cavity 1 and the red battery-plus wire in cavity 2. Check it fail-safe before the fuses go in: with F1 and F2 out, plug W01 into J1 and the battery and measure F1's input clip (BAT+ side) against a GND pad: it must read positive, about the pack voltage (≥ 6 V; a part-discharged pack reads lower). A reversed lead reads negative and, with the fuses out, has no current path; with the fuses in it would put the battery backwards across the whole board, which has no reverse-polarity protection.",
